status: in-progress
branch: feature/cbor-unknown-fields
worktree: ../okay-wt-cbor-unknown
spec: specs/codecs.md — "Compatibility between two versions" documented this as a surprise; it is a defect

why: Json.decode IGNORES a field it does not declare and Cbor.get
  REFUSES it, for the same Schema and the same value. Found by
  schema-compat, which had to give its verdict a WIRE because of it.
  Nothing chose this: no test pins the refusal and no spec states it,
  while JsonStrict — the door that IS strict — ignores unknown fields
  by design. specs/codecs.md says CBOR carries "the same content as
  JSON". Operationally the refusal is the worse half: it makes adding
  a field a breaking change for every deployed reader.

what: Cbor.In gains skipItem (every major type, with a DEPTH LIMIT —
  a skip recurses on input depth, which the schema-driven decoder
  never does, so unbounded nesting would be a new way in); the
  interpreted decoder and Staged's generated one both skip instead of
  refusing. Compat's per-wire verdicts collapse where they were only
  reporting this defect — and the docs that trumpet the asymmetry
  have to change with it, or they become a lie.

next: skipItem + depth guard, both decoders, tests, Compat, docs
